Package: deepseek-harness
Version: 0.2.1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Installed-Size: 479944
Maintainer: DeepSeek Harness Linux Port <port@localhost>
Depends: libc6, libgtk-3-0, libnss3, libnspr4, libatk1.0-0, libatk-bridge2.0-0, libcups2, libdrm2, libxkbcommon0, libxcomposite1, libxdamage1, libxfixes3, libxrandr2, libgbm1, libpango-1.0-0, libcairo2, libasound2, libatspi2.0-0, libx11-6, libxext6, libexpat1
Description: DeepSeek Harness desktop client (native linux-arm64)
 A native linux-arm64 rebuild of the DeepSeek Harness desktop client.
 .
 The upstream product ships a Windows Electron shell plus a bundled Node
 service. This package replaces the Windows shell with an Electron main
 process compiled into the official linux-arm64 runtime, and runs the
 bundled service through the same Electron binary in ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE
 mode. Nothing here is emulated: there is no Wine, no Box64, no QEMU and no
 hangover layer, and no Windows executable is ever loaded.
 .
 The renderer is served by the bundled service on a loopback HTTP origin
 and the launch cookie is seeded into the Electron session before the first
 navigation, so the desktop UI authenticates against its own backend
 without a manual login step.
 .
 If the default loopback port 19387 is already held by a stale backend (for
 example an orphan left behind by an earlier PRoot session), the launcher
 probes forward for the next free port and pins the chosen port through
 DSH_PORT, so the bundled service and the Electron shell always agree on the
 same origin. Starting the app twice therefore no longer leaves a window
 stuck on "reconnecting".
 .
 Suitable for PRoot / proot-distro containers inside Termux-like Android
 environments, where no GPU nodes and no user namespaces are available.
 .
 This build also disables the WebSocket Ping control frame on the
 multiplexed Remote stream endpoint (websocketPingEnabled defaults to
 false). Inside PRoot the Chromium renderer aborts the TCP connection with
 code 1006 as soon as it receives a Ping frame instead of replying with a
 Pong, which made the desktop UI print "connection lost" and reconnect
 every two seconds forever. Application traffic, stream multiplexing and
 peer-scope teardown are unchanged; only the keepalive probe is off.
 .
 The desktop host now also honours the DSH_PORT environment variable, so
 the launcher port fallback (when 19387 is already taken by an orphan
 backend inside PRoot) is actually propagated to the embedded host
 instead of being hardcoded to 19387.
 .
 The optional native addon subpackage @deepseek-ai/node-addon-system-linux-arm64
 was missing from earlier builds, which made any workspace or session that
 needs an exclusive file lock fail at runtime with "Cannot find module
 '@deepseek-ai/node-addon-system-linux-arm64/package.json'". The addon is now
 compiled locally from the source shipped inside node-addon-system (src/flock.c)
 against the bundled N-API headers, and installed to
 bin/glibc/system.node plus bin/musl/system.node. It is a real arm64 N-API
 shared object calling flock(2) directly; locking, EAGAIN contention and
 release-then-relock were all verified on this machine.
